# Web3Forms access keys — comma-separated, ONE KEY PER RECIPIENT INBOX.
#
# The free Web3Forms tier delivers each submission to the single verified address
# that the key was created with (the `ccemail` multi-recipient field is a paid PRO
# feature). To reach several inboxes on the free tier, create one free account per
# address and list every key here; the form posts to all of them in parallel.
#
# To get a key: go to https://web3forms.com, enter the destination email address,
# and copy the access key that gets emailed to you. Create one key per inbox that
# should receive submissions, then list them all below.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# NOTE: Vite inlines any VITE_-prefixed var into the client bundle, so these keys
# are publicly visible in the built JS. That is expected and safe for Web3Forms — an
# access key only permits sending mail to its own verified inbox and cannot read data.

VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEYS=key-for-tim,key-for-ben
